To integrate JWT-based authentication and authorization across multiple microservices running on different ports, you need to ensure that each microservice validates the JWT token passed in the request headers. Here’s a step-by-step guide on how to achieve this:

### Common JWT Validation Code

Since all your microservices need to validate the JWT token, it’s a good idea to extract common JWT validation logic into a shared library. This library can be included as a dependency in each microservice.

